Still on the 5x5 board: going off the RIGHT edge produces a raw column of 5, a positive number that is also out of range. Would plain % have worked for that case?,No - plain % fails for positive overflow too,"Yes: 5 % 5 is 0, the correct wrap. floorMod is needed specifically for the negative cases, going off the top or the left edge, where plain % returns a negative number",No - positive overflow needs a separate if-statement,"Yes, but only when the board is square",,2,"Worth being precise: floorMod is not magic, it differs from % only for negative inputs. Using it everywhere just avoids having to reason about which edge you are on.",2

