In the recorded run, a wrap-around game on a 5-row board started at (0,0) and pressed UP eight times. The heads printed were: (4,0) (3,0) (2,0) (1,0) (0,0) (4,0) (3,0) (2,0). Explain the fifth and sixth entries.,The game restarted after five moves,"From (1,0) UP gives row 0, still on the board

Real code:

public class CylinderSnakeGame extends SnakeGame {

    @Override
    protected Point handleBoundary(Point rawNewHead) {
        int row = rawNewHead.getRow();
        if (row < 0 || row >= getBoard().getHeight()) {
            return null;                            // top/bottom are fatal
        }
        int wrappedCol = Math.floorMod(rawNewHead.getCol(), getBoard().getWidth());
        return new Point(row, wrappedCol);          // left/right wrap
    }
}

CylinderSnakeGame was added later as a third boundary variant. Which files had to be modified to add it?,"SnakeGame, to add a third branch to handleBoundary","None - it is a new class extending SnakeGame and overriding one method

