public enum Direction {
    UP(-1, 0), DOWN(1, 0), LEFT(0, -1), RIGHT(0, 1);

    private final int deltaRow;
    private final int deltaCol;
}

A fourth variant is requested: a bouncing edge that reverses the snake's direction instead of killing it. Look at what handleBoundary() receives and what SnakeGame stores. Why can this hook not express that?,"It can - return the reflected position, e.g. turn row -1 into row 1","It cannot. handleBoundary() is given only the candidate position, not the direction of travel, and SnakeGame stores no direction at all - each move's direction is supplied by the caller - so there is nowhere to record 'you are now travelling the other way' for the next move","It cannot, because Math.floorMod does not support negative bouncing","It can, but only for the wrap-around subclass",,2,"Reflecting the coordinate also fails in practice: row -1 becomes row 1, which is where the snake's own neck is, so it dies instantly. Supporting bounce means changing the hook's signature - the one part of a template method that subclasses cannot fix for themselves.",2

