handleBoundary() is called at step two, before the self-collision check and before any food handling. What would go wrong if it were called last instead?,Nothing - the order of the checks does not matter,"The collision and food checks would be run against a raw position that may not be on the board at all, so a wrap-around game would compare against coordinates like (-1, 0) which no body segment or food can ever occupy",The snake would grow twice per move,The observers would be notified before the move happened,,2,"The boundary step's job is to turn a raw candidate into the real position, and every later step depends on having the real one. That is why it is pinned at step two in the fixed part of the algorithm.",2

