The abstract parent calls handleBoundary(), a method it does not implement, from inside a method it does implement. What is the direction of the call at runtime?,The parent calls its own empty version,The parent's code calls down into whichever subclass the object actually is - a ClassicSnakeGame instance runs ClassicSnakeGame's version even though the call is written in SnakeGame,The subclass calls up into the parent,The call is resolved at compile time to the first subclass in the file,,2,"The parent controls the sequence but the subclass supplies one step, which is only possible because the call is dispatched on the actual object's type at runtime.",2

